# K7 - Quanta and coupling. Kata sandbox sketch (plan section 3.6).
# [K7-nn] sketch IDs are recognised by validate_architecture / trace and ignored by the
# CI adl-coverage gate. Never [TR-*]; promotion is decided only at K12 (architecture/REVIEW.md).
DESCRIPTION K7 - the dynamic couplings between the server, the hook processes and the remote
CATEGORY System Landscape
NAMESPACE TrK7NS
DEFINE SYSTEM Total Recall K7 Sandbox AS trk7
    DEFINE COMPONENT Cross-quantum Couplings AS couplings
    DEFINE COMPONENT External Edges AS externaledges

# Course pp. 40-41: list every coupling that binds the quanta. Static ones (imports) are restricted by
# TR-S13, TR-S14 and TR-R5. The dynamic ones carry no import: a marker file one process drops for
# another (.reconcile-requested, polled every 10 s by the server, DEFAULT_POLL_MS), and a signal one
# sends to another (session-end.sh SIGTERMs the MCP child). system.adl declares the opposite
# direction (server TO hooks, server-mode-sync) and not this one.
ASSERT(Cross-quantum Couplings: every dynamic coupling found in the hook scripts (marker file, signal) has a DEFINE COMMUNICATION between the same two services in system.adl) # [K7-01]

# Course pp. 42-43, Task 3: the link to the slow, unreliable party is asynchronous, and an assertion
# keeps agents to it. The only external is the org git remote; it already is async. The check makes
# that a property instead of a coincidence.
ASSERT(External Edges: every DEFINE COMMUNICATION whose target is a DEFINE EXTERNAL carries # edge: async) # [K7-02]

# Not re-asserted, answered with existing evidence (answers.md): the quanta list in system.adl,
# static coupling across quanta (TR-S13, TR-S14, TR-R5), the sync/async label on every edge
# (adl-consistency.test.ts), the fixed 10 s poll (BACKLOG DECIDED entry).
